      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>This plant monster looks like a dead but still standing tree until it begins to move, a wicked face opening up on its side as it uses its roots to walk towards its victims, its branches flailing for their heads like grasping limbs. Sometimes also known as a “mandrake,” but it's not buried in the ground at all…- Imban</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 19, touch 9, flat-footed 19 (+10 natural, -1 Dex)</p><p>hp 68 [96] (8d8+32)</p><p>Fort +10, Ref +1, Will +3</p><p>Immune plant traits</p><p>Weakness fire</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 20 ft.</p><p>Melee slam +12 (1d8+7 plus grab and poison)</p><p>Space 5 ft.; Reach 5 ft.</p><p>Special Attacks Bad Breath</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 21, Dex 9, Con 18, Int 6, Wis 13, Cha 6</p><p>Base Atk +6; CMB +10 (+14 grapple); CMD 20</p><p>Feats Improved Natural Attack (Slam), Power Attack, Skill Focus (Perception), Weapon Focus (Slam)</p><p>Skills Perception +15</p><p>SQ Treespeech</p><h2>Ecology</h2><p>Environment mountains</p><p>Organization small group (1-3)</p><p>Treasure incidental</p>"
      }
